Type: Package
Package: LLMRpanel
Title: Calibrated Silicon Samples for Survey and Experiment Design
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ali", "Sanaei", , "sanaei@uchicago.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Quantitative silicon sampling that requires a recorded calibration
  comparison before any human-population claim, built on 'LLMR'. Persona panels
  are drawn from user-supplied population margins. Survey and experimental
  instruments, including Likert items, forced choices, open responses, vignettes,
  and conjoint tasks, are administered with item- and option-order randomization.
  Every result object carries a calibration slot and prints an UNCALIBRATED
  banner until benchmark comparison fills it. The package's stance is printed into
  its objects: silicon panels are design-stage instruments for instrument
  pretesting and power analysis, and instruments for measuring model behavior.
  They do not estimate human population quantities unless calibration earns that
  reading.
